  "about": "A speaker's label as it may be given: the name an operator reads and confirms, in any script. The worker (runtime/native_uid/identity.cpp), the carrier (plugin/native/enrollment.go) and the input schemas of speaker.enroll and speaker.associate are held to this file. labels are whole labels as UTF-8 in hexadecimal, and whether speaker.enroll takes them as a label of 1 to 128 characters. refused_code_points is the Unicode general categories Cc, Cf, Zl and Zp, whole, as inclusive hexadecimal ranges in ascending order (Unicode 16.0.0; 15.0.0 and 17.0.0 list the same); it is the table of spec/correction_vectors.json. A label holds none of them, except one of joiners standing between two characters that are neither a space (spaces: category Zs) nor a joiner. A label already stored is read as it was stored; this is what a new one may be.",
